# Exceptions to the layout limits that the organize pass could not remove. A new exception is a line here with its
# reason, in the commit that needs it. Format: <kind> <path> <reason...> (see the Tools part of CLAUDE.md).

# records plan, decision 5: its top-level flow and its -Local-gated section cannot move into a dot-sourced file without changing behaviour
file-size scripts/launch-sot.ps1 top-level flow and -Local-gated section stay in one file

# skeleton E10: entry-point paths under scripts/ are a published interface
folder-size scripts entry-point paths are a published interface

# the repo-root page is the map tier (it names the subsystems' charter folders, not every root entry); records plan, rec-12
file-list CLAUDE.md the repo-root page is the map tier, not a module page

# rust.yml's "Function length" clippy step fails a function over 100 code lines unless it carries a reasoned
# allow(clippy::too_many_lines); this pins how many rust/ holds (not rust/vt100). It can only fall: removing one lowers
# the number in the same commit.
too-many-lines rust 64 functions over 100 code lines that carry a reasoned allow
